Regression isolation rerun (2026-08-29, Asia/Shanghai)
- The formal VM repository had an uncommitted 119-line change in app/velawear_agent/drivers/velawear_pan.c. Its SHA-256 was 93f186a77f0c57b2c15efd97573aecad09879aee33b2e424cd9986a862575a0e.
- That change added Classic PAN visibility/name/class setup after BLE initialization. The corresponding image was 5,995,912 bytes with SHA-256 88736123a7191542e0b875d12e116dacbd76796df898a56133d1433bcd92f960. Two independent Windows scans found no VelaWear and matching_service=0; the BLE HIL stopped before CCCD enablement.
- For the A/B control, the formal branch version of velawear_pan.c was built in the same Ninja process. The build source SHA-256 was 0c3a202b066470834a46b88093f1ae957fbfe6bddab03d959b650593e1dc241d; the object contained no Classic PAN strings; nuttx.bin was 5,994,568 bytes with SHA-256 773d09a15be2cc469aefeed4037adf37250e29124a612af68809a62110718f16.
- The control image was flashed at 1,000,000 baud to 0x12010000 with verify. Cold boot returned BLE HCI status 0x00 for 0x2006, 0x2008, 0x2009, and 0x200a and printed advertising start ret=0.
- Windows then observed VelaWear at CDAB78563412 with RSSI -24 to -30 dBm, matching_service=7. The full HIL completed with service_status=0, all five characteristic statuses=0, cccd_status=0, threshold_before=100e, threshold_after=100e, and notifications=[000000].
- Conclusion: the BLE regression is reproduced and isolated to the uncommitted Classic PAN app change in combination with the current SiFli Bluetooth HCI adapter. The known-good control image remains on the board; the uncommitted change was not added to this submission PR.

Local Mock LLM BLE round trip (2026-08-29, Asia/Shanghai)
- Board image: known-good control image, nuttx.bin SHA-256 773d09a15be2cc469aefeed4037adf37250e29124a612af68809a62110718f16; no firmware changes were made for this test.
- Host bridge: Windows VelaWear LLM bridge connected to BLE identity CD:AB:78:56:34:12 and sent one CHAT_INPUT message: "今天有点累，陪我聊两句".
- Mock service: a loopback OpenAI-compatible HTTP endpoint returned "今天也要记得休息和喝水。" exactly once; the bridge reported bridge_exit=0.
- Mock request body used model mock-velawear and contained the board-originated prompt; this confirms the board request reached the host bridge and the response was written back over BLE.
- Concurrent 1 Mbps UART snapshot captured VelaWear boot, BLE advertising, and connected err=0x00.
- This is a local protocol/HIL proof only. It does not prove the contest-required team-maintained server, a real cloud LLM conversation, visible LCD rendering, physical touch, audible speaker output, voice wakeword, or the required demo video.

